const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"研究问题",en:"Research question"},body:{zh:"论文分析公司披露、市场流动性和资本成本之间的理论联系。 阅读时应把它理解为受样本、时点和制度限定的问题，而不是可以脱离条件的结论。",en:"The article analyzes a theoretical connection among corporate disclosure, market liquidity, and the cost of capital. Read it as a bounded question, not as a conclusion that automatically travels beyond its sample, dates, or institutional setting."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1540-6261.1991.tb04620.x",label:{zh:"The Journal of Finance (1991) · 来源说明",en:"The Journal of Finance (1991) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"研究设计",en:"Research design"},body:{zh:"它构建信息与流动性模型，将披露选择和投资者交易条件在明确假设下连接。 比较对象、观察窗口和对照关系共同构成研究合同；改变其中一项，可能改变所检验的命题。",en:"It develops an information-and-liquidity model in which disclosure choices and investor trading conditions are linked through stated assumptions. The comparison, observation window, and control relation are part of the research contract; changing one can change the proposition being tested."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1540-6261.1991.tb04620.x",label:{zh:"The Journal of Finance (1991) · 来源说明",en:"The Journal of Finance (1991) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"数据与时点",en:"Data and timing"},body:{zh:"经验延伸需带日期的披露内容与可得性、投资者或做市商信息指标、流动性定义、价格数据和披露制度规则。 字段定义、可得时点和样本筛选需要与原研究分别记录，不能仅因变量同名或使用最新修订值就视为可比。",en:"An empirical extension requires dated disclosure content and availability, investor or market-maker information measures, liquidity definitions, price data, and institutional disclosure rules. Keep fields, availability timing, and sample filters separate from the original study: a same-named variable or later-revised database is not automatically comparable."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1540-6261.1991.tb04620.x",label:{zh:"The Journal of Finance (1991) · 来源说明",en:"The Journal of Finance (1991) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"如何理解结果",en:"How to read the result"},body:{zh:"论文给出披露如何在其假设下影响流动性和资本成本的机制，并不认证某发行人的披露质量或融资成本。 它只支持来源所描述的经验或理论关系，不能把相关性、模型拟合或历史表现升级为因果、可执行性或未来保证。",en:"The paper supplies a mechanism for how disclosure can affect liquidity and capital costs under its assumptions; it does not certify any issuer's disclosure quality or financing cost. This remains the empirical or theoretical relation described by the source; it does not turn association, fit, or historical performance into causality, an executable procedure, or a future guarantee."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1540-6261.1991.tb04620.x",label:{zh:"The Journal of Finance (1991) · 来源说明",en:"The Journal of Finance (1991) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"复核清单",en:"Replication checks"},body:{zh:"区分披露事件时点和报告期；定义自愿与强制披露；保留流动性度量、投资者集合和模型的信息假设。 开展后续分析前，应将这些选择写入版本化研究记录，并保留原始来源链接与访问日期。",en:"Separate disclosure event time from reporting period; define voluntary versus mandatory disclosure; preserve liquidity measure, investor set, and the model's information assumptions. Before extending the analysis, record these choices in a versioned note and retain the primary-source link and access date."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1540-6261.1991.tb04620.x",label:{zh:"The Journal of Finance (1991) · 来源说明",en:"The Journal of Finance (1991) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"适用边界",en:"Scope boundary"},body:{zh:"该条导读引用 The Journal of Finance (1991)。理论设定不能替代审计、法律或监管评估，也不证明每个市场或披露的因果效应。 如需数值结论、参数、表格或稳健性检验，请回到原文并单独核对版本、附录与样本定义。",en:"This guide cites The Journal of Finance (1991). The theoretical setting cannot substitute for audit, legal, or regulatory evaluation and does not establish a causal effect for every market or disclosure. For numerical conclusions, parameters, tables, or robustness tests, return to the original and separately verify the edition, appendices, and sample definitions."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1540-6261.1991.tb04620.x",label:{zh:"The Journal of Finance (1991) · 来源说明",en:"The Journal of Finance (1991) · source description"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"本文只整理“Disclosure, Liquidity, and the Cost of Capital”公开说明的研究对象与设计边界，不构成收益预测、交易规则或全文复现。理论设定不能替代审计、法律或监管评估，也不证明每个市场或披露的因果效应。",en:"This guide only organizes the publicly described question and design of “Disclosure, Liquidity, and the Cost of Capital”. It is not a return forecast, trading rule, or full-text replication. The source's stated scope remains controlling."}};export{e as default};
